Creating an account level summary, segmenting our accounts to find a group level summary showing the first purchase date, last purchase date, and total revenue. We will then find the total tenure days by subtracting last by first date.

The main purpose of this section is to prepare the data first for a Kaplan-Meier Survival Analysis to understand how much our customers churn from their initial engagements. 

library(lubridate)

won_clv$Date <- mdy_hm(won_clv$Actual.Close.Date)
won_clv$Date <- as.Date(won_clv$Date)

print(class(won_clv$Date))

account_summary <- won_clv %>%
  group_by(Account) %>%
  summarise(
    first_purchase = min(Date),
    last_purchase = max(Date),
    total_revenue = sum(Actual.Revenue),
    n_transactions = n()
  ) %>%
  mutate(tenure_days = as.numeric(last_purchase - first_purchase))

After performing the account segmentation, it's worth doing a quick sanity check to confirm that variables are assigned as expected. Fortunately in R this is easy by checking the account_summary files that's appeared in our RStudio environment. We can check that tenure days and the other new columns are active and accurate.
